      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.upenn.edu/how-to-apply/international-applicants","label":"Penn: International Applicants"},{"url":"https://admissions.upenn.edu/how-to-apply/preparing-your-application/academics","label":"Penn: Academics"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["For this reason, we do not have explicit course requirements or minimum test score requirements for admittance.","Therefore, we encourage you to consistently take classes in core academic areas—English, social studies, math, science, and foreign language—throughout your four years of high school. … In applicants to the College of Arts and Sciences, we would like to see: … Strong preparation in a balanced and advanced college preparatory curriculum"],"note":"Economics BA is in the College of Arts and Sciences. Penn encourages core academic classes (English, social studies, math, science, foreign language) throughout high school and, for the College, a balanced and advanced college-preparatory curriculum — advice, not named subject requirements."},
