      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/apply-to-berkeley/first-year-applicants-uc-berkeley/freshmen-requirements/","label":"UC Berkeley: First-Year Requirements"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Students who apply to UC Berkeley should meet the following minimum requirements: Meet the A-G subject course requirements. (Review the A-G Policy Resource Guide) Have a 3.0 GPA in A-G courses taken in the 10th and 11th grade years. (3.4 GPA for non-residents)","note":"Berkeley’s minimum requirements are the A–G subjects and A–G GPA; no admissions test is required (Berkeley is test-free)."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/apply-to-berkeley/first-year-applicants-uc-berkeley/freshmen-requirements/","label":"UC Berkeley: First-Year Requirements"},{"url":"https://engineering.berkeley.edu/admissions/undergraduate-admissions/get-ready-to-apply-freshman/","label":"Berkeley Engineering: Get ready to apply – freshman"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Students who apply to UC Berkeley should meet the following minimum requirements: Meet the A-G subject course requirements. (Review the A-G Policy Resource Guide) Have a 3.0 GPA in A-G courses taken in the 10th and 11th grade years. (3.4 GPA for non-residents)","History/Social Science – 2 years English – 4 years Mathematics – 3 years (4 years including Calculus recommended for engineering) Laboratory Science – 2 years (3 years including Physics recommended for engineering) Language other than English – 2 years Visual & Performing Arts – 1 year College Preparatory Elective – 1 year (chosen from the subjects listed above or another course approved by the university)"],"note":"Official (UC A–G subject requirements): History/Social Science 2 years; English 4 years; Mathematics 3 years; Laboratory Science 2 years; Language other than English 2 years; Visual & Performing Arts 1 year; College-preparatory elective 1 year; plus a 3.0 GPA in A–G courses in grades 10–11 (3.4 for non-residents). The year counts are quoted from Berkeley Engineering’s campus page because admissions.berkeley.edu links to the UC A–G guide rather than listing them; they are the UC-wide pattern, not engineering-specific.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists the UC A–G subject requirements (and a minimum A–G GPA); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Completion of the two-year A-level programme with at least three academic exams meets Berkeley’s secondary-study requirement (IGCSE/O-levels alone do not). A-Level results are submitted for the official record once admitted.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/apply-to-berkeley/international-students/requirements-for-international-students/","label":"UC Berkeley: Requirements for International Students"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Please note: If your curriculum requires further certification (examination results such as French Baccalaureate, IGCSE, A Levels, ATAR, etc.) you will also be required to submit those for the official academic record once admitted. … The university requires further study, either completion of the two-year A-level program with a minimum of three academic exams, the IB diploma program, or another similar academic curriculum."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"The IB Diploma programme meets Berkeley’s secondary-study requirement for international applicants. IB exam scores are not required but are used as “value added” if submitted.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/apply-to-berkeley/international-students/requirements-for-international-students/","label":"UC Berkeley: Requirements for International Students"},{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/application-faqs/","label":"UC Berkeley: Application FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Please note: If your curriculum requires further certification (examination results such as French Baccalaureate, IGCSE, A Levels, ATAR, etc.) you will also be required to submit those for the official academic record once admitted. … The university requires further study, either completion of the two-year A-level program with a minimum of three academic exams, the IB diploma program, or another similar academic curriculum.","Q: Will UC Berkeley use scores from SAT subject test, AP test, IB test, etc. in the application review process? A: Yes. UC Berkeley will continue to accept additional subject test scores that will be used as “value added” in the review process. These subject tests are not required but can be submitted to demonstrate advanced proficiency in an academic subject."]},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["AP (and IB) exam scores: not required; used as “value added” in review if submitted"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/application-faqs/","label":"UC Berkeley: Application FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Q: Will UC Berkeley use scores from SAT subject test, AP test, IB test, etc. in the application review process? A: Yes. UC Berkeley will continue to accept additional subject test scores that will be used as “value added” in the review process. These subject tests are not required but can be submitted to demonstrate advanced proficiency in an academic subject."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["UC Personal Insight Questions: answer 4 of 8 (max 350 words each)","No interviews (alumni or admissions officer); InitialView materials optional for international applicants","Letters of recommendation: by invitation only, voluntary","Portfolios and unsolicited supplemental materials are not accepted"],"sources":[{"url":"https://engineering.berkeley.edu/admissions/undergraduate-admissions/get-ready-to-apply-freshman/","label":"Berkeley Engineering: Get ready to apply – freshman"},{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/apply-to-berkeley/international-students/requirements-for-international-students/","label":"UC Berkeley: Requirements for International Students"},{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/apply-to-berkeley/first-year-applicants-uc-berkeley/first-year-policy-changes/","label":"UC Berkeley: First-Year Policies"},{"url":"https://admissions.berkeley.edu/application-faqs/","label":"UC Berkeley: Application FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Students will choose 4 of the 8 questions to respond to. Each response is limited to a maximum of 350 words.","UC Berkeley does not offer alumni or admissions officer interviews as part of its application process.","Select applicants to UC Berkeley are invited to submit two letters of recommendation. Submission is voluntary and not required for full consideration of the application for admission.","A: No. Unfortunately, we are unable to accept portfolios, senior-year grades, or other supplemental materials."]}
