    "us-law-georgetown": {
      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["SAT or ACT required — all candidates, including internationally based students","At least one full SAT or ACT; superscores are not accepted","Exception: applications without scores can be accepted where a student is physically unable to access a test centre (explanation form required)"],"sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/application-requirements-and-forms/","label":"Georgetown: Application Requirements and Forms"},{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/how-to-prepare/","label":"Georgetown: Preparing for Georgetown"},{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/international-applicants/","label":"Georgetown: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Georgetown requires submission of either SAT or ACT scores as part of the application process.","Georgetown requires submission of at least one full SAT or ACT and does not accept superscores.","Georgetown University requires submission of SAT and/or ACT scores as part of our holistic application review process for all candidates, including internationally based students. In exceptional cases where students are physically unable to access an SAT or ACT test center in their area, we can accept applications without SAT or ACT scores."]},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["English proficiency test recommended, not required, for students attending a school where English is not the language of instruction","Tests accepted: Duolingo English Test, IELTS, TOEFL (PBT, iBT, IPT Plus)"],"sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/international-applicants/","label":"Georgetown: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Georgetown recommends, but does not require, results from an English language proficiency test for students who attend a school where English is not the language of instruction. Georgetown accepts results from the DET (Duolingo English Test), IELTS, or TOEFL® (PBT, iBT® and IPT® Plus versions), to fulfill this recommendation.","note":"Georgetown’s pages state no minimum English test scores."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/application-requirements-and-forms/","label":"Georgetown: Application Requirements and Forms"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Required High School-submitted materials include: High school transcript School profile Counselor letter of recommendation","note":"Georgetown’s first-year requirements list school materials, recommendations, SAT/ACT, essays and an alumni interview; no course-specific admissions test."},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/how-to-prepare/","label":"Georgetown: Preparing for Georgetown"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"In order to prepare for a Georgetown education, all applicants are expected to have completed four years of English, a minimum of two years of social studies, language study, and mathematics, and one year of natural science.","note":"Official: all applicants are expected to have completed four years of English, a minimum of two years of social studies, language study and mathematics, and one year of natural science. Government is in the College of Arts & Sciences (humanities/social sciences); Georgetown lists no extra preparation for it.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists expected high-school coursework (4 years English; at least 2 years social studies, language and mathematics; 1 year natural science); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Applicants whose school system includes A-Level final examinations must submit projected and/or final results with the application, sent directly by the secondary school.","sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/international-applicants/","label":"Georgetown: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you will graduate from an educational system that includes final examinations such as A-Levels, International Baccalaureate, or the French Baccalaureat, you will need to submit projected and/or final results as part of the application process. These results must be submitted to our office directly from your secondary school (and eventually from the testing agency if enrolling at Georgetown)."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"Applicants whose school system includes International Baccalaureate final examinations must submit projected and/or final results with the application, sent directly by the secondary school.","sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/international-applicants/","label":"Georgetown: International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If you will graduate from an educational system that includes final examinations such as A-Levels, International Baccalaureate, or the French Baccalaureat, you will need to submit projected and/or final results as part of the application process. These results must be submitted to our office directly from your secondary school (and eventually from the testing agency if enrolling at Georgetown)."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: submission of AP scores is highly recommended for students who have taken AP exams (not required)"],"sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/application-requirements-and-forms/","label":"Georgetown: Application Requirements and Forms"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"For students that have taken AP exams, we highly recommend submission of these scores as part of the application process.","note":"Georgetown’s AP/IB credit policies (after enrolling) are not admission requirements and are not recorded here."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Apply directly to one of Georgetown’s six undergraduate schools (Government: College of Arts & Sciences)","Writing supplement: two short essays and two long essays, including a school-specific essay","Alumni interview: required when assigned; some internationally based students may not be assigned one"],"sources":[{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/","label":"Georgetown: First Year Applicants"},{"url":"https://uadmissions.georgetown.edu/apply/first-year-applicants/application-requirements-and-forms/","label":"Georgetown: Application Requirements and Forms"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Applicants are required to apply directly to one of Georgetown’s six undergraduate schools.","Georgetown requires submission of two short essays and two long essays: … Students are required to complete their interview when assigned. Some internationally-based students may not be assigned an interview due to availability."]}
    },
