      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/index.html","label":"Northwestern: Apply"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Required for First Year Students … Northwestern supplement (with additional writing supplements) … Optional and Program-Specific … SAT and/or ACT scores"},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/faqs/high-school-courses/index.html","label":"Northwestern: High School Courses FAQs"},{"url":"https://www.mccormick.northwestern.edu/computer-science/academics/undergraduate/","label":"Northwestern McCormick: Computer Science Undergraduate"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["The McCormick School of Engineering and Applied Science encourages strong preparation in mathematics and science. Recommended coursework includes:","The Department of Computer Science within the McCormick School of Engineering offers the following undergraduate degrees: … Bachelor of Science in Computer Science … Bachelor of Arts in Computer Science through the Weinberg College of Arts and Sciences"],"note":"Official: The McCormick School of Engineering and Applied Science encourages strong preparation in mathematics and science. Recommended coursework: English 4 full-year courses; laboratory science at least 3 full-year courses (chemistry and physics preferred); mathematics 3.5–4 full-year courses (calculus preferred, if available; the minimum includes 2 full-year courses of algebra, 1 of plane geometry and 1 semester of trigonometry); 5–6 additional full-year courses including foreign language, history and social sciences. These are recommendations, not requirements. The Computer Science BS is offered by McCormick (the BA is through Weinberg).","reviewFlag":"Official source lists recommended high-school coursework for McCormick (math 3.5–4 years, calculus preferred; lab science 3 years, chemistry and physics preferred; English 4 years); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"partial","accepted":"unknown","detail":"Where secondary school completion is contingent on external exam scores, Northwestern requires those scores; other subject-based external results are treated as useful but optional.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/faqs/standardized-testing-policy/index.html","label":"Northwestern: Standardized Testing Policy FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"As in the past, we will treat subject-based external test results (i.e. APs, supplemental IBs, etc.) as useful but optional information, knowing these exams and curricula are unavailable to many students around the world. For students whose secondary school completion is contingent on external exam scores, we will continue to require them.","note":"Northwestern’s admissions pages do not name A-Levels — this row applies its general statement on external exam scores."},
      "ib": {"status":"verified","accepted":"yes","detail":"IB scores are optional and may be self-reported for consideration in the review; where secondary school completion is contingent on external exam scores (e.g. the IB Diploma), Northwestern requires them.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/faqs/standardized-testing-policy/index.html","label":"Northwestern: Standardized Testing Policy FAQs"},{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/faqs/standardized-testing-policy/index.html","label":"Northwestern: Standardized Testing Policy FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Whether or not a student chooses to submit an SAT or ACT score, that student may submit additional, optional forms of testing (e.g., Advanced Placement or International Baccalaureate scores) for consideration in the review process.","As in the past, we will treat subject-based external test results (i.e. APs, supplemental IBs, etc.) as useful but optional information, knowing these exams and curricula are unavailable to many students around the world. For students whose secondary school completion is contingent on external exam scores, we will continue to require them."],"note":"The “contingent on external exam scores” rule is stated generally; the page does not name the IB Diploma in that sentence."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["Advanced Placement: AP scores are optional and may be self-reported for consideration in the review"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/faqs/standardized-testing-policy/index.html","label":"Northwestern: Standardized Testing Policy FAQs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Northwestern also considers other optional forms of testing (AP, IB, etc.) and students may self-report those scores as well."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Northwestern writing supplement required (one 300-word question; up to two optional short questions encouraged)","Applicants apply to one of Northwestern’s undergraduate schools; the same review criteria apply to all","No alumni interviews; InitialView interviews accepted (optional) from students at international high schools"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/requirements.html","label":"Northwestern: Application Materials"},{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/advice/academic-path.html","label":"Northwestern: Your Academic Path"},{"url":"https://admissions.northwestern.edu/apply/requirements.html","label":"Northwestern: Application Materials"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["The following question is required for all Common Application and Coalition with Scoir applicants (optional for QuestBridge applicants). Please respond in 300 words or fewer:","Northwestern requires all applicants to apply to one of the six undergraduate schools. There is no strategic advantage to applying to any specific school, as we use the same admission review criteria for all Northwestern undergraduate applicants.","Northwestern no longer offers alumni interviews as an optional part of the application process. … For students applying from international high schools, Northwestern accepts interviews from InitialView. Similar to Glimpse videos, InitialView interviews are not required and applicants without one are at no disadvantage in our review process."]}
