    "us-economics-vanderbilt": {
      "satAct": {"status":"verified","items":["Test-optional for fall 2027 and fall 2028 entry — applies to first-year, transfer, international and homeschool applicants","Applicants choose on the application whether to be considered with or without ACT/SAT scores; the choice does not advantage or disadvantage review","ACT or SAT will be required from fall 2029 entry"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/testing-policies/","label":"Vanderbilt: Testing Policies"},{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/testing-policies/","label":"Vanderbilt: Testing Policies"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Vanderbilt University will continue its test-optional policy for students applying for undergraduate admission to the classes entering in the fall of 2027 or 2028. For students applying for undergraduate admission to the class entering in the fall of 2029 and beyond, Vanderbilt will require standardized testing scores.","Students applying for fall 2027 and 2028 will indicate on the application whether they wish to be considered with or without ACT or SAT scores. The applicant’s choice regarding ACT or SAT score submission will not advantage or disadvantage the application review."]},
      "englishLanguage": {"status":"verified","items":["English proficiency test results required from international applicants, if applicable — not required where first language or language of instruction is English","Waived with ACT English above 26 or SAT Evidence-Based Reading and Writing above 630","Recommended minimum scores (not cut-offs): TOEFL iBT 5, TOEFL Essentials 10.5, IELTS 7.0, Cambridge C1 Advanced/C2 Proficiency 185, LanguageCert 75, Duolingo 130"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Official results of the TOEFL iBT (including Home and Paper Editions), TOEFL Essentials, IELTS, Cambridge English C1 Advanced or C2 Proficiency, LanguageCert, or Duolingo English Test, if applicable. See recommended minimum score chart below. … Applicants whose first language or language of instruction is English are not required to submit English proficiency exam scores. … Applicants who score above 26 on the ACT English section or above 630 on the SAT Evidence-based Reading and Writing section are not required to submit English proficiency exam scores. … Test Recommended minimum score TOEFL iBT 5 TOEFL Essentials 10.5 IELTS 7.0 Cambridge English C1 Advanced or C2 Proficiency 185 LanguageCert 75 Duolingo English Test 130","note":"Vanderbilt labels these \"recommended minimum\" scores. The TOEFL iBT figure (5) is on the new 1–6 TOEFL band scale."},
      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Required Application Materials All required parts of the Common Application or Coalition, powered by Scoir, including the personal essay and short answer $50 nonrefundable application fee, or fee waiver for qualified students Official high school transcript Counselor letter of recommendation Two academic teacher letters of recommendation"},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Since Vanderbilt uses a holistic admissions review process, we do not have minimum coursework requirements. Most successful candidates will present a curriculum that includes the equivalent of five academic subjects each year for four years. Recommended course work includes 4 units of English, 4 units of mathematics, 4 units of natural science, 2 units of foreign language, 2 units of social science/humanities, and 4 units of additional course work in these areas, or other academic courses such as engineering science, computer science, social science or natural science research, or advanced work in the humanities.","note":"Official: Vanderbilt has no minimum coursework requirements; recommended coursework is 4 units of English, 4 of mathematics, 4 of natural science, 2 of foreign language, 2 of social science/humanities, plus 4 additional units in these or other academic areas. Applies to all Vanderbilt first-year applicants.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists recommended high-school coursework (4 English, 4 maths, 4 natural science, 2 foreign language, 2 social science/humanities); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision."},
      "aLevel": {"status":"partial","accepted":"unknown","detail":"International applicants must submit an official high school transcript with all classes and grades to date; leaving-exam results alone do not complete the application.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Applicants must submit an official high school transcript, including all high school classes and grades or marks to date. Submitting only leaving exams will not complete your application.","note":"Vanderbilt’s admissions pages do not mention A-Levels by name — this row applies its general statement on leaving exams. (A-Level credit after enrolment is a catalog matter, not admission.)"},
      "ib": {"status":"partial","accepted":"unknown","detail":"Vanderbilt recommends taking IB (or AP/honours) courses where the school offers them, as appropriate.","sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/expert-advice/","label":"Vanderbilt: Expert Advice"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If your high school offers advanced, honors, Advanced Placement, or International Baccalaureate courses it's recommended you pursue those as appropriate.","note":"Vanderbilt’s admissions pages say nothing about IB Diploma scores or predicted IB grades in admission; the IB 6/7 statement on the FAQ is about college credit after enrolling, not admission."},
      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["AP exam scores (and SAT Subject Test scores) may be self-reported and may be considered in review — optional"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/testing-policies/","label":"Vanderbilt: Testing Policies"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"If students self-report scores from AP exams or SAT Subject tests, these may be considered as part of the review process."},
      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["No admissions interviews","Optional video: Glimpse (U.S. high school students who are U.S. citizens, including undocumented students) or InitialView interview (international / non-U.S. citizens)","Required: personal essay and short answer"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"},{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Vanderbilt does not offer interviews through the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. Through partnerships with Glimpse and InitialView, Vanderbilt offers optional video submission opportunities for applicants.","Required Application Materials All required parts of the Common Application or Coalition, powered by Scoir, including the personal essay and short answer $50 nonrefundable application fee, or fee waiver for qualified students Official high school transcript Counselor letter of recommendation Two academic teacher letters of recommendation"]}
    },
