      "admissionsTests": {"status":"verified","none":true,"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":"Required Application Materials All required parts of the Common Application or Coalition, powered by Scoir, including the personal essay and short answer $50 nonrefundable application fee, or fee waiver for qualified students Official high school transcript Counselor letter of recommendation Two academic teacher letters of recommendation"},
      "subjectPrerequisites": {"status":"partial","items":["Not used in Altiora’s matching yet — see the note for the official guidance"],"codes":[],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.vanderbilt.edu/apply/first-year-process/","label":"Vanderbilt: Application Process: First-year"},{"url":"https://computing.vanderbilt.edu/undergraduate-programs/","label":"Vanderbilt: College of Connected Computing — Undergraduate Programs"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Since Vanderbilt uses a holistic admissions review process, we do not have minimum coursework requirements. Most successful candidates will present a curriculum that includes the equivalent of five academic subjects each year for four years. Recommended course work includes 4 units of English, 4 units of mathematics, 4 units of natural science, 2 units of foreign language, 2 units of social science/humanities, and 4 units of additional course work in these areas, or other academic courses such as engineering science, computer science, social science or natural science research, or advanced work in the humanities. … It is highly recommended that candidates applying to the School of Engineering have taken calculus, calculus-based physics, and chemistry.","Vanderbilt’s first new college in 40 years unites computer science, data science and scientific computing under one roof"],"note":"Official: Vanderbilt has no minimum coursework requirements; recommended coursework is 4 units of English, 4 of mathematics, 4 of natural science, 2 of foreign language, 2 of social science/humanities, plus 4 additional units. Vanderbilt also highly recommends calculus, calculus-based physics and chemistry for School of Engineering applicants; the Computer Science B.S. is now listed under the College of Connected Computing, and no page says whether that recommendation applies to it.","reviewFlag":"Official source lists recommended high-school coursework (4 English, 4 maths, 4 natural science, 2 foreign language, 2 social science/humanities); data/courseRequirements.js holds none. Owner decision. Check whether the School of Engineering calculus/physics/chemistry recommendation applies to the CS B.S. (College of Connected Computing)."},
