      "otherQualifications": {"status":"verified","items":["AP exam scores optional and considered if submitted","Applicants from schools outside the U.S. may submit three AP exam scores under the testing options — one in math for McKelvey Engineering, Olin Business and Arts & Sciences STEM applicants"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.washu.edu/how-to-apply/what-were-looking-for/","label":"WashU: What We’re Looking For"},{"url":"https://admissions.washu.edu/how-to-apply/first-year-international-applicants/","label":"WashU: First-Year International Applicants"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["Additionally, whether you decide to include the SAT or ACT in your application, we’re happy to consider scores on AP exams or predicted scores on A-Levels or IB exams for students in those curricula.","For both non-U.S. citizens and U.S. citizens applying from a high school outside of the United States, you may choose to submit the following: SAT; or ACT; or Predicted or actual results from national examinations, such as the Baccalauréat, Abitur, Maturita, etc.; or Predicted or actual results for the International Baccalaureate (IB) Diploma; or Predicted or actual A-Levels; or Three (3) AP Exam scores; or One exam score must be in math for students applying to the following schools: STEM majors in the College of Arts & Sciences, McKelvey School of Engineering, Olin Business School Three (3) IB higher-level exam scores if not an IB Diploma candidate; or One must be an HL Math score for students applying to the following schools: STEM majors in the College of Arts & Sciences, McKelvey School of Engineering, Olin Business School"]},
