      "otherRequirements": {"status":"verified","items":["Common App personal essay (UNC’s two short-answer supplemental questions were removed for 2026–27)","One letter of recommendation from a teacher in a core academic area","All students begin in the College of Arts and Sciences; intended major does not affect admission"],"sources":[{"url":"https://admissions.unc.edu/short-essays-removed-from-carolinas-2026-2027-application/","label":"UNC: Short essays removed from Carolina’s 2026-2027 application"},{"url":"https://admissions.unc.edu/apply/types-of-applications/first-year/","label":"UNC: First-Year Application"},{"url":"https://admissions.unc.edu/faqs/how-does-my-intended-major-affect-my-application/","label":"UNC: How does my intended major affect my application?"}],"lastVerified":"2026-10-19","sourceSnippet":["As the 2026-2027 application period approaches, we’re removing the two short answer supplemental questions. … The required Common Application essay, extracurricular activities, and additional information sections will continue to be spaces where students can share their voice and passions.","This letter should come from a teacher who taught you in a core academic area, like English, math, science, social science, or world language.","At Carolina, you’ll begin your studies in the College of Arts and Sciences, where you’ll explore your interests, build on your strengths, and develop your skills for citizenship, leadership, lifelong learning, and the careers of the future. … Your selections won’t affect your admission in any way."]}
